 Aid Visit Why Scripps College Scripps College Facts FAQs Contact Us Academic Experience Faculty Majors & Minors Academic Resources Accommodations and Academic Resource Services Clark Humanities Museum Department of Natural Sciences European Union Center Humanities Institute Intercollegiate Feminist Center Library Registrar Scripps College Press Williamson Gallery Post-Bacc Program Research Study Abroad Life & Community Creating Community Leadership Center Residential Vibrancy Student Services Contact Us CARE@SCRIPPS Career Planning & Resources Tiernan Field House Title IX Close Search Scripps College Search Working at Scripps College Faculty Positions Visiting Assistant Professor in German Studies Fall 2027/Spring 2028 October 7, 2026 Visiting Assistant Professor in German Studies Fall 2027/Spring 2028 Faculty Positions Scripps College, a women’s liberal arts college with a strong interdisciplinary tradition, invites applications for a non-tenure-track, full-time position as Visiting Assistant Professor to teach in the Department of German Studies for the 2027–28 academic year, beginning July 1, 2027, with the possibility of reappointment for 2028–29 pending review and approval. The Visiting Assistant Professor will read senior theses and teach five courses per academic year, including at least three language courses as well as at least one upper division content course (literature, film, culture etc.) conducted in German. ABD required, Ph.D. preferred. The successful candidate will shape the future of language acquisition in the department and, therefore, have demonstrable experience and expertise as well as substantial training in foreign language pedagogy. In addition, we are looking for an individual with a strong commitment to undergraduate liberal arts education. Applicants for the Visiting Assistant Professor position should upload a cover letter, CV, three letters of reference, and teaching evaluations from three courses online ( https://apply.interfolio.com/195181 ) by December 15, 2026. Please direct any questions about this position to Kevin Vennemann  ( [email protected] ), Chair, German Studies. The salary for this position will range from $67,500 to $75,000 and will be based on a variety of factors, including but not limited to internal equity, experience, education, specialty, and training. In light of recent federal updates to visa processing and associated costs, the College is generally not in a position to sponsor visas for faculty appointments. Scripps College is one of seven members of The Claremont Colleges Consortium located 35 miles east of Los Angeles. In keeping with its ongoing commitment to build and support an inclusive academic community, Scripps College seeks applicants who will actively support Scripps College’s Principles of Community and Institutional Values. Tags About Scripps Visit Campus Apply Now 1030 Columbia Avenue Claremont, CA 91711 (909) 621-8000 Campus Map Virtual Tour Diversity Centennial Celebration Strategic Plan Employment Scripps Forward: Centennial Campaign Scripps Merchandise Emergency Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Higher Education Emergency Relief Fund (HEERF) Campus Hazing Transparency Report The Claremont Colleges . © Scripps College | Accessibility | Nondiscrimination Statement | Privacy"
